# Phase 10: tooltips (shift shows every line), the guide, sounds
ldtd.tooltip.more=Hold Shift for more
tile.ldtd.hearth.tip1=Claims the land around it. Raids come for it at night.
tile.ldtd.hearth.tip2=Use: open the stockpile the Hearth-sprites build from.
tile.ldtd.hearth.tip3=Sneak-use, empty hand: its state; again to call a raid early.
tile.ldtd.hearth.tip4=Use with Duskglass: raise its level.
item.ldtd.blueprint.tip1=Hold to see where it will go; use inside your territory.
item.ldtd.blueprint.tip2=Hearth-sprites build it from the stockpile.
item.ldtd.duskglass.tip1=Dropped by the Gloam and paid for every raid survived.
item.ldtd.duskglass.tip2=Feed it to a Hearth to raise its level.
item.ldtd.duskglass.tip3=Sneak-use a tower's core with it to upgrade the tower.
item.ldtd.command_brand.tip1=Orders the Ember Guards within 32 blocks.
item.ldtd.command_brand.tip2=Use on a block: hold there. On a Gloam: attack it.
item.ldtd.command_brand.tip3=Sneak-use: follow me. Use at the air: back to the post.
tile.ldtd.tower_core.tip1=The heart of a tower. Built by a blueprint.
tile.ldtd.tower_core.tip2=Sneak-use with Duskglass to upgrade; break it to salvage half.
tile.ldtd.dusk_stone.tip1=The stone of the Dusk Spires.
tile.ldtd.spire_core.tip1=A Dusk Spire's heart. Break it to raze the spire.
commands.hearth.guide.usage=/hearth guide
commands.hearth.guide.given=Here is the Hearthkeeper's Guide.

ldtd.guide.1.title=The Hearthkeeper's Guide
ldtd.guide.1.1=The Gloam come by night, and they hunt flame.
ldtd.guide.1.2=A Hearth holds them back. Set one down where you mean to stay.
ldtd.guide.2.title=Your Hearth
ldtd.guide.2.1=Its land is your territory. Only there can towers stand, and only there can the Gloam break blocks.
ldtd.guide.2.2=Sneak-use it, empty-handed: its state. Again: call a raid early.
ldtd.guide.3.title=Stockpile & Sprites
ldtd.guide.3.1=Use the Hearth to open its stockpile. Fill it with stone, planks and more.
ldtd.guide.3.2=Hearth-sprites build your orders from it, and mend the damage.
ldtd.guide.4.title=Blueprints
ldtd.guide.4.1=Craft a blueprint for a wall or tower. Hold it to see a ghost of the build; use it in your territory.
ldtd.guide.4.2=The sprites build it from the stockpile.
ldtd.guide.5.title=Towers
ldtd.guide.5.1=Archer: steady shots.
ldtd.guide.5.2=Cannon: hits a crowd.
ldtd.guide.5.3=Frost: slows them all.
ldtd.guide.5.4=Lantern: light weakens the Gloam.
ldtd.guide.5.5=Guard Post: Ember Guards. A Command Brand gives orders.
ldtd.guide.5.6=Flare: downs fliers, and lights them up.
ldtd.guide.6.title=Raids
ldtd.guide.6.1=On nights you are near, the Gloam gather at your border.
ldtd.guide.6.2=Each one at the Hearth drains its Flame. If it goes out, the Hearth falls dark: relight it with coal.
ldtd.guide.7.title=Duskglass
ldtd.guide.7.1=The Gloam drop it, and each raid survived pays some.
ldtd.guide.7.2=Feed it to the Hearth to grow it. Sneak-use a tower core with it to upgrade the tower.
ldtd.guide.8.title=Dusk Spires
ldtd.guide.8.1=Black spires in the wilds feed the raids on Hearths near them.
ldtd.guide.8.2=Break the core at a spire's foot to raze it. After three, the Eclipse comes.
ldtd.guide.9.title=Neighbours
ldtd.guide.9.1=A village may keep an unclaimed Hearth: sneak-use it to take it up.
ldtd.guide.9.2=/hearth trust <name> shares yours. /hearth guide: a new copy.
ldtd.guide.10.title=Learn More
ldtd.guide.10.1=Every tower, Gloam, raid and number is in the LDTD Wiki.
ldtd.guide.10.2=Open the LDTD Wiki
